WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:02.440
Hello, internet. I'm Gav.

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:03.420
I'm Dan.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.510
We've been trying to do this video

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:05.343
for a long time.

00:00:05.343 --> 00:00:07.100
Last time we tried it, this happened.

00:00:09.322 --> 00:00:10.405
Oh, my god!

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.200
I burned my hand, didn't I?

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.190
Yeah, you did.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.660
So now we have changed location,

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.630
we've got a more powerful cooker

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:19.580
and it's really windy,

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.360
which makes it even more dangerous

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.360
than the last time we did it.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:24.420
So, basically, this
video is what not to do

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.260
in an oil fire situation.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.430
If you have a load of that is on fire,

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:29.500
don't throw water on it,

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.988
because the water sinks through the oil,

00:00:30.988 --> 00:00:33.820
evaporates immediately
on the surface of the pan

00:00:34.836 --> 00:00:36.500
and throws all the oil upwards

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.180
in a big flaming, hot, melty mess.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:40.013
And you'll burn, yeah.

00:00:40.013 --> 00:00:40.846
You will burn.

00:00:40.846 --> 00:00:42.420
So I'm taking more precautions this time

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:43.840
with a face mask

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.483
and standing up-wind of the fire.

00:00:50.548 --> 00:00:52.100
All right.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.033
Get that oil on.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:58.960
That's enough.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:00.530
Bloody hell!

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:01.413
You reckon?

00:01:01.413 --> 00:01:02.916
Yeah.

00:01:02.916 --> 00:01:04.066
It's on fire?

00:01:04.066 --> 00:01:05.040
Yeah.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.443
Bloody hell.

00:01:06.443 --> 00:01:08.009
Get the propane out then.

00:01:08.009 --> 00:01:11.426
Okay, that's it.

00:01:15.387 --> 00:01:16.220
Go for it.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:01.430
Dan, that was amazing.

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:02.400
Yeah, it's unbelievable.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:03.790
Amazing, slash terrifying.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:04.623
Scary.

00:03:04.623 --> 00:03:05.456
You may have noticed

00:03:05.456 --> 00:03:07.440
that we are actually
five thousand miles away

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:08.960
from where we shot that video.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:10.966
But, it's quieter here.

00:03:10.966 --> 00:03:11.822
And it's greener.

00:03:11.822 --> 00:03:12.669
And there's less wind.

00:03:12.669 --> 00:03:13.502
Our original audio was ,

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:15.213
wind noise.

00:03:15.213 --> 00:03:16.630
So, we are doing another outro.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:19.180
If you wanna put out an oil fire,

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:20.380
don't throw water on it.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:23.170
Soak a towel, a dish towel or a tea towel,

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:25.030
put it over the top of the pan

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.210
and it should go out.

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:27.820
Also, don't, sort of, pour the oil

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:30.160
onto your hand, like I
did in the previous video.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:30.993
Don't do that either.

00:03:30.993 --> 00:03:32.078
Right there.

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:33.161
That was right over there.

00:03:33.161 --> 00:03:33.994
Yeah. Don't do that.

00:03:33.994 --> 00:03:36.540
Feel free to use this in a fire-training,

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.500
educational video, if you
see this and want to use it.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:40.620
That's fine.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.860
Follow us on Twitter if you want.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:45.230
Buy a shirt. We got free shirts.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:47.830
And we will see you in the next video.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:48.830
Thanks for watching.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:03:59.394
How's your scar now?

00:03:59.394 --> 00:04:00.557
It's not too bad. Oh, no, it's this hand.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.167
Look, you can see it still.

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:04.000
Let's have a look.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.462
Let's have a close-up.

00:04:05.462 --> 00:04:06.824
It's like this circle
here is the main patch.

00:04:06.824 --> 00:04:08.124
It healed up well.

00:04:08.124 --> 00:04:08.957
Yeah, not bad.

00:04:08.957 --> 00:04:09.790
I'm impressed with it.

